  "id": "Compound::DB00887 - Gene::10864",
  "verbalization": "Bumetanide is implicated in the transport of organic anions, as evidenced by its binding to Slc22a11, which is involved in organic anion transport. This transport process is further mediated by Slc22a7, suggesting a potential role for Bumetanide in the regulation of anion transport through Slc22a7. The evidence is supported by the direct interaction between Bumetanide and Slc22a11, followed by the involvement of Slc22a7 in the transport process. The presence of Oxytetracycline as a binding partner to Slc22a11 adds another layer of complexity, indicating that Bumetanide may influence the functional state of Slc22a11 through interactions with other compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Bumetanide affects Slc22a7, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
